Assignment 3
uptime - Check system load

nproc

top-htop     
Looks for:
%CPU → process using too much CPU
%MEM → memory-heavy process
Any process constantly taking > 90% CPU
Zombie process
High I/O wait (wa > 10–15%)

iostat -xz 1
Checks for I/O (disk bottleneck)

free -m
Look for low free memory and high swap usage.
If swap is heavily used → add RAM or find memory-leaking processes.

mpstat -P ALL 1
Check CPU core usage

iotop 
Processes doing heavy disk I/O.

netstat -plant | grep :80 | wc -l 
Count active web connections.

ss -tulnp 
Check open ports and listening processes.

tail -n 50 /var/log/syslog 
Check system logs for errors.

dmesg | tail 
Kernel-level warnings/errors.
